-- FSL-168 (plan-20261118): drop the enterprise tables and the `session` enterprise columns.
--
-- Statements generated by `drizzle-kit generate`; only their order is changed by hand.
-- The generator emits the `DROP TABLE ... CASCADE` statements first, whose CASCADE already
-- removes the two `session` foreign keys, so its later `DROP CONSTRAINT` of those keys fails
-- (42704). As the card requires, the `session` CHECK, foreign keys, unique index and the four
-- columns go first, then the 20 enterprise tables. Forward-only: the tables and their rows
-- cannot be restored (ADR-FSL-13).
